sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To circumscribe a square about a given circle.
----
proof:

Let {ABCD} be the given circle.

It is required to circumscribe a square about the circle {ABCD}.

Draw two diameters {AC} and {BD} of the circle {ABCD} at right angles to one another. [!just III.1, I.11]

<div class="just"><a href="/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII16/#cor">III.16,Cor</a></div>

Draw {FG}, {GH}, {HK}, and {KF} through the points {A}, {B}, {C}, and {D} touching the circle {ABCD}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="290" height="290" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="IV.7 diagram" src="propIV7.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // The two diameters at right angles, the four tangents, the right
    // angles at the points of contact (III.18), the parallels (I.28, I.30),
    // the parallelograms and their equal sides (I.34), then the right
    // angles at the corners.
    //
    // Everything added leaves the resting figure as it was. FG, GH, HK and
    // KF are solid black lines over the sides of Joyce's square, hidden at
    // rest (initiallyHidden): they give the four tangents strokes of their
    // own, and the square's face lands only on the slide that calls it a
    // square. FGHK is a transparent twin of the square for the slides that
    // name the quadrilateral before then. EA (the radius to the point of
    // contact) and the parallelograms the proof names by their diagonals —
    // GC, AK, FB, BK (the halves), GK (the whole, which is FGHK) and the
    // quarter GBEA — are transparent highlight targets with explicit ;0
    // faces.
    //
    // Right angles are red squares: AEB at the center (the diameters are
    // drawn at right angles), the two angles at each point of contact
    // (pinned small, side by side, out of ring stepping), and the four
    // corners of the square.
    var GIVEN = ["ABCD"];
    var DIAM  = GIVEN.concat(["AC","BD","A","B","C","D","rtE"]);
    var TAN   = DIAM.concat(["FG","GH","HK","KF","F","G","H","K"]);
    var RAD   = TAN.concat(["E","EA"]);
    var RTA   = RAD.concat(["rtA1","rtA2"]);
    var RTALL = RTA.concat(["rtB1","rtB2","rtC1","rtC2","rtD1","rtD2"]);
    var PGM   = RTALL.concat(["FGHK","pgGC","pgAK","pgFB","pgBK"]);
    var QUAR  = PGM.concat(["GBEA","rtG"]);
    var CORN  = QUAR.concat(["rtH","rtK","rtF"]);
    var DONE  = CORN.concat(["square"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "IV.7",
        pivot: "E",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;145,40",
            "C;point;free;145,250",
            "E;point;midpoint;A,C;black;green",
            "B;point;perpendicular;E,A",
            "D;point;perpendicular;E,C",
            "F;point;parallelogram;A,E,D",
            "G;point;parallelogram;B,E,A",
            "H;point;parallelogram;C,E,B",
            "K;point;parallelogram;D,E,C",
            "square;polygon;quadrilateral;F,G,H,K;0;0;black;random",
            "ABCD;circle;radius;E,A;0;0;black;random",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C",
            "BD;line;connect;B,D",
            // The four tangents, hidden at rest (see above).
            "FG;line;connect;F,G",
            "GH;line;connect;G,H",
            "HK;line;connect;H,K",
            "KF;line;connect;K,F",
            // The radius to the point of contact at A.
            "EA;line;connect;E,A;0;0;0",
            // The quadrilateral, the parallelograms, and the quarter GBEA.
            "FGHK;polygon;quadrilateral;F,G,H,K;0;0;0;0",
            "pgGC;polygon;quadrilateral;G,H,C,A;0;0;0;0",
            "pgAK;polygon;quadrilateral;A,C,K,F;0;0;0;0",
            "pgFB;polygon;quadrilateral;F,G,B,D;0;0;0;0",
            "pgBK;polygon;quadrilateral;B,H,K,D;0;0;0;0",
            "GBEA;polygon;quadrilateral;G,B,E,A;0;0;0;0",
            "rtE;sector;angleMarkerRight;E,A,B;0;0;red;red",
            "rtA1;sector;angleMarkerRight;A,G,E,12;0;0;red;red",
            "rtA2;sector;angleMarkerRight;A,F,E,12;0;0;red;red",
            "rtB1;sector;angleMarkerRight;B,G,E,12;0;0;red;red",
            "rtB2;sector;angleMarkerRight;B,H,E,12;0;0;red;red",
            "rtC1;sector;angleMarkerRight;C,H,E,12;0;0;red;red",
            "rtC2;sector;angleMarkerRight;C,K,E,12;0;0;red;red",
            "rtD1;sector;angleMarkerRight;D,K,E,12;0;0;red;red",
            "rtD2;sector;angleMarkerRight;D,F,E,12;0;0;red;red",
            "rtG;sector;angleMarkerRight;G,A,B;0;0;red;red",
            "rtH;sector;angleMarkerRight;H,B,C;0;0;red;red",
            "rtK;sector;angleMarkerRight;K,C,D;0;0;red;red",
            "rtF;sector;angleMarkerRight;F,D,A;0;0;red;red"
        ],
        // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A and C, free. They are
        // the circle's points, but the proof introduces them only with the
        // diameters, so both are deferred and follow `visible`. B, D
        // (perpendicular), E (midpoint) and F, G, H, K (parallelogram) are
        // derived and listed per slide. The resting figure is unaffected.
        deferDraggables: ["A","C"],
        initiallyHidden: ["FG","GH","HK","KF"],
        aliases: { "GF": "FG", "HG": "GH", "KH": "HK", "FK": "KF",
                   "AE": "EA", "BED": "BD", "DB": "BD", "CA": "AC",
                   "GK": "FGHK",
                   "AEB": "rtE", "BEA": "rtE",
                   "EBG": "rtB1", "GBE": "rtB1",
                   "AGB": "rtG", "BGA": "rtG" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“To circumscribe a square about a given circle.”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["ABCD"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "IV.7" }] },
            { text: "Let {ABCD} be the given circle.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["ABCD"] },
            { text: "It is required to circumscribe a square about the circle {ABCD}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["ABCD"] },
            { text: "Draw two diameters {AC} and {BD} of the circle {ABCD} at right angles to one another.",
              visible: DIAM,
              highlighted: ["AC","BD"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "AC",  name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "BD",  name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "rtE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [
                  { claim: "a diameter through the center", ref: "III.1" },
                  { claim: "at right angles to one another", ref: "I.11" } ] },
            { text: "Draw {FG}, {GH}, {HK}, and {KF} through the points {A}, {B}, {C}, and {D} touching the circle {ABCD}.",
              visible: TAN,
              highlighted: ["A","B","C","D"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "FG", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "GH", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "HK", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "KF", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "at right angles to the diameters at A, B, C, D", ref: "III.16,Cor" }] },
            { text: "Then, since {FG} touches the circle {ABCD},",
              visible: TAN,
              highlighted: ["FG","ABCD"] },
            { text: "and {EA} has been joined from the center {E} to the point of contact at {A},",
              visible: RAD,
              highlighted: ["EA","E","A"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "E", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "therefore the angles at A are right.",
              visible: RTA,
              highlighted: ["rtA1","rtA2"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "rtA1", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "rtA2", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "a radius to the point of contact is perpendicular to the tangent", ref: "III.18" }] },
            { text: "For the same reason the angles at the points {B}, {C}, and {D} are also right.",
              visible: RTALL,
              highlighted: ["rtB1","rtB2","rtC1","rtC2","rtD1","rtD2"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "rtB1", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "rtB2", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "rtC1", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "rtC2", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "rtD1", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "rtD2", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "III.18" }] },
            { text: "Now, since the angle {AEB} is right, and the angle {EBG} is also right,",
              visible: RTALL,
              highlighted: ["rtE","rtB1"] },
            { text: "therefore {GH} is parallel to {AC}.",
              visible: RTALL,
              highlighted: ["GH","AC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "GH parallel to AC", ref: "I.28" }] },
            { text: "For the same reason {AC} is also parallel to {FK},",
              visible: RTALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","KF","rtD2"] },
            { text: "so that {GH} is also parallel to {FK}.",
              visible: RTALL,
              highlighted: ["GH","KF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "parallel to the same straight line AC", ref: "I.30" }] },
            { text: "Similarly we can prove that each of the straight lines {GF} and {HK} is parallel to {BED}.",
              visible: RTALL,
              highlighted: ["FG","HK","BD"] },
            { text: "Therefore {GK}, {GC|pgGC}, {AK|pgAK}, {FB|pgFB}, and {BK|pgBK} are parallelograms,",
              visible: PGM,
              highlighted: ["FGHK","pgGC","pgAK","pgFB","pgBK"] },
            { text: "therefore {GF} equals {HK}, and {GH} equals {FK}.",
              visible: PGM,
              highlighted: ["FG","HK","GH","KF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "opposite sides of a parallelogram are equal", ref: "I.34" }] },
            { text: "And, since {AC} equals {BD}, and {AC} also equals each of the straight lines {GH} and {FK},",
              visible: PGM,
              highlighted: ["AC","BD","GH","KF"] },
            { text: "and {BD} equals each of the straight lines {GF} and {HK},",
              visible: PGM,
              highlighted: ["BD","FG","HK"] },
            { text: "therefore the quadrilateral {FGHK} is equilateral.",
              visible: PGM,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH","HK","KF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "opposite sides of a parallelogram are equal", ref: "I.34" }] },
            { text: "I say next that it is also right-angled.",
              visible: PGM,
              highlighted: ["FGHK"] },
            { text: "For, since {GBEA} is a parallelogram, and the angle {AEB} is right, therefore the angle {AGB} is also right.",
              visible: QUAR,
              highlighted: ["GBEA","rtE","rtG"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "rtG", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "opposite angles of a parallelogram are equal", ref: "I.34" }] },
            { text: "Similarly we can prove that the angles at {H}, {K}, and {F} are also right.",
              visible: CORN,
              highlighted: ["rtH","rtK","rtF"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "rtH", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "rtK", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "rtF", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "Therefore {FGHK} is right-angled.",
              visible: CORN,
              highlighted: ["rtG","rtH","rtK","rtF"] },
            { text: "But it was also proved equilateral, therefore it is a square, and it has been circumscribed about the circle {ABCD}.",
              visible: DONE,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH","HK","KF"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "square", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "Therefore a square has been circumscribed about the given circle.",
              visible: DONE,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH","HK","KF","rtG","rtH","rtK","rtF"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.F." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "IV.7") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.11":       "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI11/",
        "I.28":       "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI28/",
        "I.30":       "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI30/",
        "I.34":       "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI34/",
        "III.1":      "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII1/",
        "III.16,Cor": "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII16/#cor",
        "III.18":     "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII18/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Then, since {FG} touches the circle {ABCD}, and {EA} has been joined from the center {E} to the point of contact at {A}, therefore the angles at A are right. For the same reason the angles at the points {B}, {C}, and {D} are also right. [!just III.18]

Now, since the angle {AEB} is right, and the angle {EBG} is also right, therefore {GH} is parallel to {AC}. [!just I.28]

For the same reason {AC} is also parallel to {FK}, so that {GH} is also parallel to {FK}. [!just I.30]

Similarly we can prove that each of the straight lines {GF} and {HK} is parallel to {BED}.

Therefore {GK}, {GC|pgGC}, {AK|pgAK}, {FB|pgFB}, and {BK|pgBK} are parallelograms, therefore {GF} equals {HK}, and {GH} equals {FK}. [!just I.34]

And, since {AC} equals {BD}, and {AC} also equals each of the straight lines {GH} and {FK}, and {BD} equals each of the straight lines {GF} and {HK}, therefore the quadrilateral {FGHK} is equilateral. [!just I.34]

I say next that it is also right-angled.

For, since {GBEA} is a parallelogram, and the angle {AEB} is right, therefore the angle {AGB} is also right. [!just I.34]

Similarly we can prove that the angles at {H}, {K}, and {F} are also right. Therefore {FGHK} is right-angled.

But it was also proved equilateral, therefore it is a square, and it has been circumscribed about the circle {ABCD}.

Therefore a square has been circumscribed about the given circle.

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
----
guide: This proposition is used in @XII.10.
